# {{ projectName }}

A typed Python command-line starting point. Typer owns parsing and completion;
Pydantic Settings owns lazy configuration validation. Add application scenarios
behind the CLI when the project's requirements are defined.

## 🚀 Quick start

Requires Python 3.12+ and uv. Resolve and commit the first lock, then use Docker.

```bash
uv lock
make check build verify
```

After installation, `{{ projectName }} --help`, `{{ projectName }} --version`
and `python -m {{ packageName }} --version` work outside the checkout.
`{{ projectName }} config show --limit 0 --no-enabled` is read-only.
Explicit CLI values override `{{ packageName | upper }}_` environment variables,
then an explicitly selected `--config file.env`, then defaults. No ambient dotenv
file, HOME configuration, secret directory or database is loaded at import.
An omitted option does not override env; explicit false and zero do. Null is
invalid for these required bool/int settings. No machine JSON output is added.

## 🧭 Architecture

The [architecture note](docs/architecture.md) describes the CLI/settings boundary.
Project-specific decisions belong in [PROJECT.md](PROJECT.md). Keep application
modules and tests outside managed `tests/foundation/` so Copier updates preserve them.

## 🧪 Testing

`make check` runs locked lint, strict types, pytest and statement/branch reports.
Coverage percentages are advisory; failing tests, builds and broken reports fail.
`make verify` installs the built wheel in a separate container and runs the tests
without checkout sources, including the executable and module subprocess checks.

## 📚 Documentation

Read [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for commands. Copier writes source/ref in
`.copier-answers.yml`; update only from a clean checkout with a reviewed immutable
ref and inspect conflicts. Template version and application version are independent.

## 📄 License policy

Copier records `licensePolicy` and, for MIT, the project owner's holder/year.
The default `unlicensed` choice grants no project redistribution license.
[Scaffold attribution and dependency terms](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) remain separate.
Existing owner license files survive updates.
